The October 10 import-path conflicts are resolved; GitHub currently reports `mergeable=true`. The parser fix remains unchanged (4 files, +188/-10). The latest author-reported local validation is 29 passing tests across the two parser test files, plus passing `ruff check` and `ruff format --check`. The timing tests are regression guards, not a performance reproduction on every machine.

The previous contributor-count gate has cleared: this head's `pre-run-check` log reports `verified label=false, ready label=false, 4+ merged PRs=true`, and both `pre-run-check` and `pre-commit` succeeded. I could not find a Buildkite result for this head. Since passing that gate does not itself grant CI-command authorization, I am requesting an authorized upstream CI run. Thank you!

